{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>The sons of Uzziel, the cousins of Aaron.</b> Rashi, of blessed memory, explained that Uzziel was the brother of Amram, as it is said (Exodus 6:18): ״ובני קהת עמרם ויצהר וחברון ועזיאל״. And what did the Master, of blessed memory, come to teach us — for did we not already know that Uzziel was the brother of Amram? Rather, his explanation itself requires explanation: for this reason Scripture mentioned 'the cousins of Aaron' (דודי אהרן), to make known that Uzziel and Aaron were alike in their deeds, one to the other. And Scripture juxtaposed Uzziel to Aaron: just as Aaron was a lover of peace and a pursuer of peace, so too Uzziel was a lover of peace and a pursuer of peace. And the Master, of blessed memory, did not need to explain that Uzziel was the brother of Amram except for the sake of <b>the cousins of Aaron</b>."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:24:25.679533757Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}